IMPORT prelude

-- HDB flat schemes AS PUBLISHED: the Fiance/Fiancee Scheme and the Single Singapore Citizen Scheme for a new flat bought
-- from HDB, the Enhanced CPF Housing Grant (Singles), and the minimum occupation period (MOP) of a new flat.
--
-- SOURCES. Housing & Development Board (HDB) web pages, all read on 12 October 2026 (the text of each page was read in a
-- browser; the pages carry no "last updated" date):
--   (1) "Couples and Families", tab "Fiance and fiancee":
--       https://www.hdb.gov.sg/buying-a-flat/flat-grant-and-loan-eligibility/couples-and-families
--   (2) "Singles", tab "Singles":
--       https://www.hdb.gov.sg/buying-a-flat/flat-grant-and-loan-eligibility/singles
--   (3) "Enhanced CPF Housing Grant for Singles", and the PDF table it links, "average gross monthly income and
--       corresponding EHG amount" (3 pages):
--       https://www.hdb.gov.sg/buying-a-flat/flat-grant-and-loan-eligibility/singles/enhanced-cpf-housing-grant
--       https://www.hdb.gov.sg/-/media/buying-a-flat/flat-grant-and-loan-eligibility/singles/enhanced-cpf-housing-grant/EHG-amount-Singles.pdf
--   (4) "Conditions After Buying a New Flat" (the MOP):
--       https://www.hdb.gov.sg/buying-a-flat/bto-sbf-and-open-booking-of-flats/conditions-after-buying-a-new-flat
--
-- AS PUBLISHED, NOT LAW. None of this is legislation. These are HDB's eligibility conditions and grant rules as its website
-- states them. They change by announcement, without a Bill or a gazetted instrument, and the site keeps no dated history.
-- So every figure here is "as published on 12 October 2026" unless the page itself gives a date; the only figure with a
-- page-given date is the EHG (Singles) "From 20 August 2024". The pages cite no statute. HDB sells flats under Part 4 of
-- the Housing and Development Act 1959 (row subjects/sg/housing-and-development-act-1959): s 50 (restrictions as to
-- purchase) and s 55(1), which bars sale "within the prescribed minimum occupation period" without the Board's consent.
-- This row supplies the period as HDB publishes it; the statutory tests stay in the Act's row.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for three requirements in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl:
--   REQ-0007 (cradle-to-grave-simone e050, 2028-02-20): an engaged couple apply for a new 4-room flat under the
--            Fiance/Fiancee Scheme; are they eligible, and by when must they marry?
--   REQ-0018 (cradle-to-grave-simone e07c, 2036-08-15): keys collected 15 August 2031 to a new Standard 4-room flat; from
--            what date may it be sold?
--   REQ-0274 (cradle-to-grave-jun-hao j074, 2042-02-18): a single citizen of 35 earning $2,800 a month applies for a new
--            2-room Flexi flat; eligible, and what grant?
-- The scenario dates are in the future; the encoding answers on the policy as published in October 2026.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: resale flats and resale grants; the multi-generation, orphaned-siblings, non-resident-family, seniors and
-- short-lease 2-room Flexi routes; the $24,000 extended-family ceiling; SPR households (3 years' SPR status) and the
-- $10,000 premium; a fiance(e) under 21 (who may only be a core occupier); undischarged bankrupts; the resale levy and
-- subsidy recovery; the HDB Flat Eligibility (HFE) letter process itself; how "income" is assessed (an input); the EHG
-- (Singles) table for an applicant with a non-resident spouse (the PDF's second page extracts with its columns
-- misaligned, so it was not transcribed); the pro-rating of the EHG for a lease that does not cover the youngest core
-- member to age 95; MOP periods excluded because the owners did not live in the flat; what "legal completion" of a new
-- flat is (taken here as key collection, an inference -- see NOTES.md finding 2).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Written in one pass from the pages above, in the style of the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `HDB flat schemes, as published on 12 October 2026`

DECLARE FlatType IS ONE OF
    `2-room Flexi`
    `3-room`
    `4-room`
    `5-room`
    `3Gen`
    `executive`

-- Page (4): a new flat is Standard, Plus or Prime; "unclassified" flats are those sold before the October 2024 sales
-- exercise and not so classified. Prime includes Prime Location Public Housing (PLH) flats sold before then.
DECLARE Classification IS ONE OF
    `Standard`
    `Plus`
    `Prime`
    `unclassified`

§§ `Calendar helpers (no source; the civil calendar)`

-- A date is written as the number yyyymmdd, e.g. 20310815 for 15 August 2031.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date` y m d MEANS
    y TIMES 10000 PLUS m TIMES 100 PLUS d

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0 AND (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0)))
    OR  y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` y m MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

§§ `Common conditions for a new flat from HDB (pages (1) and (2))`

-- Private residential property: every applicant and occupier "Must not own or have an interest in" any local or overseas
-- private residential property, and must not have disposed of one in the 30 months before the HFE letter application,
-- counted from the legal completion date of the disposal. Page (2)'s worked example: disposal on 1 July 2024, HFE letter
-- application on or after 1 January 2027.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the private property wait in months` MEANS 30

GIVEN `owns private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has disposed of private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since that disposal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the private property condition is met` IF
        (NOT `owns private residential property`)
    AND (    (NOT `has disposed of private residential property`)
          OR `months since that disposal` AT LEAST `the private property wait in months`)

-- Non-residential property: the household may own or have an interest in up to 1 at the HFE letter application.
GIVEN `non-residential properties owned` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the non-residential property condition is met` IF
    `non-residential properties owned` AT MOST 1

§§ `The Fiance/Fiancee Scheme, new flat (page (1))`

-- Flat type: "Up to a 5-room flat". A 3Gen flat goes through the multi-generation route instead.
GIVEN f IS A FlatType
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fiance couple may apply for the flat type` f IF
    CONSIDER f
        WHEN `2-room Flexi` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `3-room` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `4-room` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `5-room` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Monthly household income ceiling (total income of all persons in the HFE letter application), new flats:
--   2-room Flexi (99-year lease): $8,000;
--   3-room: $16,000 or $8,000 "depending on project" (the sales-launch press release says which);
--   4- and 5-room: $16,000.
-- As published on 12 October 2026; no effective date given. 0 means no new flat of that type under this scheme.
GIVEN f IS A FlatType, `the 3-room project has the $8,000 ceiling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family income ceiling for a new flat` f `the 3-room project has the $8,000 ceiling` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
        WHEN `2-room Flexi` THEN 8000
        WHEN `3-room` THEN IF `the 3-room project has the $8,000 ceiling` THEN 8000 ELSE 16000
        WHEN `4-room` THEN 16000
        WHEN `5-room` THEN 16000
        OTHERWISE 0

-- Citizenship: "Be a Singapore Citizen (SC)" and include at least 1 other SC or SPR. Age: at least 21 (both, for both to
-- be applicants). Previous subsidies: a household with a core member who has taken 2 housing subsidies may not buy from
-- HDB; one subsidy makes a second-timer, who pays a resale levy but may apply.
GIVEN `citizens among the couple` IS A NUMBER,
      `permanent residents among the couple` IS A NUMBER,
      `age of the elder` IS A NUMBER,
      `age of the younger` IS A NUMBER,
      `household monthly income` IS A NUMBER,
      `flat type` IS A FlatType,
      `the 3-room project has the $8,000 ceiling` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owns private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has disposed of private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since that disposal` IS A NUMBER,
      `non-residential properties owned` IS A NUMBER,
      `most housing subsidies taken by a core member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the couple may apply under the Fiance Fiancee Scheme` IF
        `a fiance couple may apply for the flat type` `flat type`
    AND `citizens among the couple` AT LEAST 1
    AND `citizens among the couple` PLUS `permanent residents among the couple` AT LEAST 2
    AND `age of the elder` AT LEAST 21
    AND `age of the younger` AT LEAST 21
    AND `household monthly income` AT MOST `the family income ceiling for a new flat` `flat type` `the 3-room project has the $8,000 ceiling`
    AND `the private property condition is met` `owns private residential property` `has disposed of private residential property` `months since that disposal`
    AND `the non-residential property condition is met` `non-residential properties owned`
    AND `most housing subsidies taken by a core member` AT MOST 1

-- Solemnisation: "You need to solemnise your marriage within 3 months from the completion of the flat purchase". HDB "may
-- request" a copy of the marriage certificate; a marriage registered overseas must be shown by a copy of its certificate
-- within the same 3 months.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months allowed to solemnise the marriage` MEANS 3

-- The last day to solemnise, given the completion date (y m d) of the flat purchase. ENCODER'S CONVENTION, not HDB's: the
-- same day of the month 3 months on, or the last day of that month if it is shorter.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day to solemnise the marriage` y m d MEANS
    IF m PLUS `the months allowed to solemnise the marriage` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN `the date` (y PLUS 1) (m PLUS 3 MINUS 12) (`the smaller of` d (`the days in month` (y PLUS 1) (m PLUS 3 MINUS 12)))
    ELSE `the date` y (m PLUS 3) (`the smaller of` d (`the days in month` y (m PLUS 3)))

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `The Single Singapore Citizen Scheme, new flat (page (2))`

-- A single is a Singapore citizen who is unmarried, widowed or divorced. New flat: a 2-room Flexi flat only; SC; "At least
-- 35 years old" (the age-21 route for widows and orphans is for resale flats only); household income ceiling for a 2-room
-- Flexi flat (99-year lease) $8,000; only first-timers ("Only first-timer core member may qualify"); the property
-- conditions as for families.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the singles minimum age for a new flat` MEANS 35

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the singles income ceiling for a new 2-room Flexi flat` MEANS 8000

GIVEN `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is married` IS A BOOLEAN,
      age IS A NUMBER,
      `household monthly income` IS A NUMBER,
      `flat type` IS A FlatType,
      `owns private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has disposed of private residential property` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months since that disposal` IS A NUMBER,
      `non-residential properties owned` IS A NUMBER,
      `housing subsidies taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the single may apply for a new flat` IF
        `is a citizen`
    AND (NOT `is married`)
    AND age AT LEAST `the singles minimum age for a new flat`
    AND (CONSIDER `flat type`
            WHEN `2-room Flexi` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `household monthly income` AT MOST `the singles income ceiling for a new 2-room Flexi flat`
    AND `the private property condition is met` `owns private residential property` `has disposed of private residential property` `months since that disposal`
    AND `the non-residential property condition is met` `non-residential properties owned`
    AND `housing subsidies taken` EQUALS 0

-- Page (2): for a new flat bought by singles, an additional $15,000 is "incorporated into the price of the booked flat".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional amount payable by singles for a new flat` MEANS 15000

§§ `The Enhanced CPF Housing Grant (Singles), new flat (page (3))`

-- "From 20 August 2024" first-timer singles may get up to $60,000; two or more singles up to $120,000 in all. The page
-- gives no earlier table, so the amounts below are for an HFE letter application on or after that date only.
GIVEN `HFE application date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the published EHG table applies` `HFE application date` IF
    `HFE application date` AT LEAST 20240820

-- Eligibility for a single buying a flat from HDB: first-timer, aged 35 or more, buying alone or with other first-timer
-- single citizens; has worked continuously for at least 12 months (the 12-month period ends 2 months before the HFE letter
-- application) and is working at the application; average gross monthly household income over the months worked in that
-- period not above $4,500 (alone) or $9,000 (with other singles); remaining lease more than 20 years; the property
-- conditions as for the flat.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EHG income ceiling for a single alone` MEANS 4500

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EHG income ceiling for two or more singles` MEANS 9000

GIVEN `is a first-timer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      age IS A NUMBER,
      `buying with other singles` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `worked continuously for 12 months and working at application` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `average monthly household income` IS A NUMBER,
      `remaining lease in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `the property conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the single qualifies for the EHG` IF
        `is a first-timer`
    AND age AT LEAST 35
    AND `worked continuously for 12 months and working at application`
    AND `average monthly household income` AT MOST
            (IF `buying with other singles`
             THEN `the EHG income ceiling for two or more singles`
             ELSE `the EHG income ceiling for a single alone`)
    AND `remaining lease in years` GREATER THAN 20
    AND `the property conditions are met`

-- The PDF, page 1 ("single applicant/ single child aged 35 or above buying with parents"): the grant by the single's
-- average monthly income. Bands of $250 from $750 to $4,500; nothing above $4,500.
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EHG for a single alone` income MEANS
    IF income AT MOST 750 THEN 60000
    ELSE IF income AT MOST 1000 THEN 55000
     ELSE IF income AT MOST 1250 THEN 52500
      ELSE IF income AT MOST 1500 THEN 47500
       ELSE IF income AT MOST 1750 THEN 45000
        ELSE IF income AT MOST 2000 THEN 40000
         ELSE IF income AT MOST 2250 THEN 35000
          ELSE IF income AT MOST 2500 THEN 32500
           ELSE IF income AT MOST 2750 THEN 27500
            ELSE IF income AT MOST 3000 THEN 25000
             ELSE IF income AT MOST 3250 THEN 20000
              ELSE IF income AT MOST 3500 THEN 15000
               ELSE IF income AT MOST 3750 THEN 12500
                ELSE IF income AT MOST 4000 THEN 10000
                 ELSE IF income AT MOST 4250 THEN 5000
                  ELSE IF income AT MOST 4500 THEN 2500
                   ELSE 0

-- The PDF, page 3 ("two or more first-timer singles"): the grant for the household by its average monthly income. Bands
-- of $500 from $1,500 to $9,000. Up to 2 singles each receive a share (page (3)).
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EHG for two or more singles` income MEANS
    IF income AT MOST 1500 THEN 120000
    ELSE IF income AT MOST 2000 THEN 110000
     ELSE IF income AT MOST 2500 THEN 105000
      ELSE IF income AT MOST 3000 THEN 95000
       ELSE IF income AT MOST 3500 THEN 90000
        ELSE IF income AT MOST 4000 THEN 80000
         ELSE IF income AT MOST 4500 THEN 70000
          ELSE IF income AT MOST 5000 THEN 65000
           ELSE IF income AT MOST 5500 THEN 55000
            ELSE IF income AT MOST 6000 THEN 50000
             ELSE IF income AT MOST 6500 THEN 40000
              ELSE IF income AT MOST 7000 THEN 30000
               ELSE IF income AT MOST 7500 THEN 25000
                ELSE IF income AT MOST 8000 THEN 20000
                 ELSE IF income AT MOST 8500 THEN 10000
                  ELSE IF income AT MOST 9000 THEN 5000
                   ELSE 0

-- The grant a single receives: nil unless eligible and the published table applies.
GIVEN `is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN, `HFE application date` IS A NUMBER, `buying with other singles` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `average monthly household income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the EHG (Singles) for the household` `is eligible` `HFE application date` `buying with other singles` `average monthly household income` MEANS
    IF `is eligible` AND `the published EHG table applies` `HFE application date`
    THEN IF `buying with other singles`
         THEN `the EHG for two or more singles` `average monthly household income`
         ELSE `the EHG for a single alone` `average monthly household income`
    ELSE 0

§§ `The minimum occupation period of a new flat (page (4))`

-- Page (4): an unclassified or Standard flat, 5 years; a Plus or Prime flat, 10 years; a flat bought under the Fresh Start
-- Housing Scheme, 20 years. Until the MOP ends the owners may not sell on the open market, rent out the whole flat, apply
-- for an HFE letter, or acquire private property. As published on 12 October 2026; no effective date given.
GIVEN c IS A Classification, `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum occupation period in years` c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` MEANS
    IF `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme`
    THEN 20
    ELSE CONSIDER c
            WHEN `Plus` THEN 10
            WHEN `Prime` THEN 10
            OTHERWISE 5

-- The MOP "starts from the legal completion date of your flat purchase". For a new flat this encoding takes that to be
-- key collection (an inference; NOTES.md finding 2). The first day the flat may be sold on the open market is the
-- anniversary of completion that many years on. ENCODER'S CONVENTION, not HDB's: from 29 February, in a year that is not
-- a leap year, the first day is 1 March.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, c IS A Classification, `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` y m d c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 2 AND d EQUALS 29 AND (NOT (`is a leap year` (y PLUS `the minimum occupation period in years` c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme`)))
    THEN `the date` (y PLUS `the minimum occupation period in years` c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme`) 3 1
    ELSE `the date` (y PLUS `the minimum occupation period in years` c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme`) m d

-- Whether, on a given date (yyyymmdd), the MOP has ended. Assumes no excluded period (the MOP excludes time when the owners
-- did not live in the flat; not encoded).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, c IS A Classification, `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day asked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the MOP has ended` y m d c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme` `the day asked` IF
    `the day asked` AT LEAST `the first day the flat may be sold on the open market` y m d c `bought under the Fresh Start Housing Scheme`
